    "https://usask.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/14/home/requisition/15693?c=usask": {
      "title": "Graduate Research Assistant, School for the Arts, Drama",
      "description": "Graduate Research Assistant, School for the Arts, Drama | Job Details University of Saskatchewan Careers P A WS Current Opportunities Benefits Relocating Tips for Applying Sign In Create Profile English (US) Graduate Research Assistant, School for the Arts, Drama Saskatoon, SK, Canada | req15693 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/16/2026 Back to Search Graduate Research Assistant, School for the Arts, Drama In the appointment of Research Assistant, your general duties and responsibilities will be: Example: Ethics applications, qualitative data analysis (Thematic Analysis), preparing reports, writing papers, designing and leading in-studio exercises for data collection,  literature/library research, administrative tasks and provision of other research support and assistance. Your general location of work will be John Mitchell Building and you will report to Shannon Blanchet, Associate Professor, School for the Arts, Drama. Required Number of Hours: 4 hours per week Duration of Employment: November 10, 2026 – June 30, 2027 Qualifications (Skills and Abilities) i.e. Minimum of a Bachelor of Arts or Bachelor of Fine Arts degree in Drama, Psychology, Anthropology, or Sociology. Knowledge and experience in ensemble-based performance practices is highly preferred. You must be registered in a graduate program. To Apply : Interested applicants must include the following in their application: cover letter, curriculum vitae and references. Send your application materials to: Shannon.blanchet@usask.ca no later than November 10, 2026. Where a graduate student is appointed to this position, it will be in-scope of PSAC. Department: School for the Arts, Drama. Supervisor Job Title: Associate Professor Status: Casual Employment Group: Graduate Students - PSAC Rate of Pay: Current rates of pay Posted Date: 10/16/2026 Closing Date: 10/23/2026 Number of Openings: 1 Work Location: On Campus #LI-DNI The University of Saskatchewan aspires to be what the world nee